# /sound: the notice for every argument form, the settings each write leaves,
# and the terminal bells each level rings. Both start with sound off -- fx by
# the harness's own FX_SOUND=0, xfx by XFX_SOUND=off -- and both ask before a
# write. fx's TMPDIR is a directory it cannot write, so its cues fall back to
# the terminal bell rather than a chime through /usr/bin/afplay (see the
# header of capture.sh): the bell is the thing being compared.
gateway sound-turns.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask XFX_SOUND=off
wait 3
home start
type first question
key Enter
wait 3
snap turn-off
bells turn-off
type /sound
key Enter
wait 1
snap bare
home bare
type /sound on
key Enter
wait 1
snap on
home on
type /sound max
key Enter
wait 1
snap max
home max
type /sound off
key Enter
wait 1
snap off
home off
type /sound
key Enter
wait 1
snap bare2
home bare2
type /sound bogus
key Enter
wait 1
snap bogus
home bogus
bells before-turn
type second question
key Enter
wait 3
snap turn-on
bells turn-on
type write the file
key Enter
wait 3
snap ask
bells ask
key 1
wait 3
snap answered
bells answered
type /sound off
key Enter
wait 1
snap off2
home off2
type fourth question
key Enter
wait 3
snap turn-off2
bells turn-off2
